<title>UK: Dixons says OFT clears Link sale to Cellnet.</title>
<headline>Dixons says OFT clears Link sale to Cellnet.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer Dixons Group Plc said on Friday the Office of Fair Trading had cleared the sale of its 40 percent stake in Link, its mobile phone business, to Telecom Securicor Cellular Radio Ltd (Cellnet).</p>
<p>Formal completion of the deal is expected within the next seven working days, Dixons said in a statement.</p>
<p>Cellnet will pay an initial 25 million stg in cash with a further payment of up to 32 million dependent largely on the performance and expansion of Link over the next five years.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
